column70:
 which means that the existence of the "else" part is mostly superfluous.  So if you have code that looks like:

```c
if (a) {
     return A();
} else if (b) {
    return B();
}
return C();
```

You can symmetrize it by doing something like:

```c
if (a) {
     return A();
} else if (b) {
    return B();
} else {
    return C();
}
```

Or alternately:

```c
if (a) {
     return A();
}
if (b) {
    return B();
}
return C();
```"}

