 because you need to swap that MPU region on task change. It also mean we need to create a new __nocache_user__ macro to put the variables in the right sections.

The other short term alternatives is to disable the D-Cache (but not the I-Cache) when `CONFIG_UART_ASYNC_API=y`. 

An other STM32 specific short term alternative is to create `__dma_alloc__` macro that allocates the variables in the DTCM. In the longer term we can imagine to let users choose between allocating those variables in the DTCM or in standard memory with the use of cache management operations."}

column59:
 "body": "Looks good. Now let's restructure the commits. 

We tend to update `west.yml` in a separate commit. You can check `git log` and see how @chrta has done it. The commit updating `west.yml` should be followed up by a single commit adding BRD4255A radio board.

You can either do it using `git rebase -i` or start from scratch by means of `git reset`. To reuse an existing commit message when redoing the commit you can `git commit --reuse-message=<commit>`. At the end you'll need to force push your updates."}

